Oh, great.  Yet another undocumented (feature?).  All the Guidebook says on
the subject is that "The other benefits of explore mode are left for the
trepid reader to discover."  I, for one, am not amused.  I'm playing discover
mode in order to learn all of the stupid mistakes one can make, in order to
have greater success when I play "real" games.  I'm actually upset that there
are such major gameplay differences--after all, the wand of wishing(3) and the
immortality are more-than-sufficient advantages for most people.

Now that I actually bother to look at the code, it's clear that only wizards
and those in discovery mode are allowed to create particular monsters.

Now I'm going to have to grep through the ENTIRETY of the code looking for
any other strategies of mine that will be invalidated by such gratuitous
differences.  Feh.

